      "content": "#include \"knn.h\"\n#include <omp.h>\n\nchar knn(int n_groups, Group * groups, int k, Point to_evaluate) {\n    char * global_labels = (char *) malloc(sizeof(char) * k);\n    float * global_dists = (float *) malloc(sizeof(float) * k);\n    int * global_gidx = (int *) malloc(sizeof(int) * k);\n    int * global_ptidx = (int *) malloc(sizeof(int) * k);\n\n    for (int i = 0; i < k; i++) {\n        global_labels[i] = -1;\n        global_dists[i] = -1.0f;\n        global_gidx[i] = -1;\n        global_ptidx[i] = -1;\n    }\n\n    #pragma omp parallel\n    {\n        char local_labels[k];\n        float local_dists[k];\n        int local_gidx[k];\n        int local_ptidx[k];\n\n        for (int i = 0; i < k; i++) {\n            local_labels[i] = -1;\n            local_dists[i] = -1.0f;\n            local_gidx[i] = -1;\n            local_ptidx[i] = -1;\n        }\n\n        #pragma omp for schedule(dynamic) nowait\n        for (int gi = 0; gi < n_groups; gi++) {\n            Group g = groups[gi];\n            for (int pj = 0; pj < g.length; pj++) {\n                float d = euclidean_distance_no_sqrt(to_evaluate, g.points[pj]);\n\n                int pos;\n                for (pos = 0; pos < k; pos++) {\n                    if (local_dists[pos] == -1.0f) break;\n                    if (d < local_dists[pos]) break;\n                    // equal distance: do not insert (preserve earlier point)\n                }\n\n                if (pos < k) {\n                    for (int y = k - 1; y > pos; y--) {\n                        local_dists[y] = local_dists[y - 1];\n                        local_labels[y] = local_labels[y - 1];\n                        local_gidx[y] = local_gidx[y - 1];\n                        local_ptidx[y] = local_ptidx[y - 1];\n                    }\n                    local_dists[pos] = d;\n                    local_labels[pos] = g.label;\n                    local_gidx[pos] = gi;\n                    local_ptidx[pos] = pj;\n                }\n            }\n        }\n\n        #pragma omp critical\n        {\n            for (int li = 0; li < k && local_dists[li] != -1.0f; li++) {\n                float d = local_dists[li];\n                char lab = local_labels[li];\n                int gidx = local_gidx[li];\n                int pidx = local_ptidx[li];\n\n                int pos;\n                for (pos = 0; pos < k; pos++) {\n                    if (global_dists[pos] == -1.0f) break;\n                    if (d < global_dists[pos]) break;\n                    if (d == global_dists[pos]) {\n                        // tie-breaking: earlier group/point index wins\n                        if (gidx < global_gidx[pos]) break;\n                        if (gidx == global_gidx[pos] && pidx < global_ptidx[pos]) break;\n                    }\n                }\n\n                if (pos < k) {\n                    for (int y = k - 1; y > pos; y--) {\n                        global_dists[y] = global_dists[y - 1];\n                        global_labels[y] = global_labels[y - 1];\n                        global_gidx[y] = global_gidx[y - 1];\n                        global_ptidx[y] = global_ptidx[y - 1];\n                    }\n                    global_dists[pos] = d;\n                    global_labels[pos] = lab;\n                    global_gidx[pos] = gidx;\n                    global_ptidx[pos] = pidx;\n                }\n            }\n        }\n    }\n\n    qsort(global_labels, k, sizeof(char), compare_for_sort);\n\n    char most_frequent = global_labels[0];\n    int most_frequent_count = 1;\n    int current_frequency = 1;\n\n    for (int i = 1; i < k; i++) {\n        if (global_labels[i] != global_labels[i - 1]) {\n            if (current_frequency > most_frequent_count) {\n                most_frequent = global_labels[i - 1];\n                most_frequent_count = current_frequency;\n            }\n            current_frequency = 1;\n        } else {\n            current_frequency++;\n        }\n\n        if (i == k - 1 && current_frequency > most_frequent_count) {\n            most_frequent = global_labels[i - 1];\n            most_frequent_count = current_frequency;\n        }\n    }\n\n    free(global_labels);\n    free(global_dists);\n    free(global_gidx);\n    free(global_ptidx);\n\n    return most_frequent;\n}\n\nint main() {\n    int n_groups = parse_number_of_groups();\n    \n    Group * groups = (Group *) malloc(sizeof(Group) * n_groups);\n\n    for (int i = 0; i < n_groups; i++) {\n        groups[i] = parse_next_group();\n    }\n\n    int k = parse_k();\n\n    Point to_evaluate = parse_point();\n\n    printf(\"%c\", knn(n_groups, groups, k, to_evaluate));\n}\n",
      "path": "src/knn.c"
    }
  ],
  "hypothesis": "Using OpenMP parallel for with schedule(dynamic) over groups distributes variable-length group computations evenly across threads; each thread maintains a private top-k array storing distance, label, and global point indices for deterministic tie-breaking. After the loop, per-thread arrays are merged into a global top-k via a critical section, preserving exact sequential output order.",
  "notes": "This approach aims to balance load across variable-length groups while maintaining correctness via tie-breaking by group and point indices. The merge in a critical section is lightweight because each thread contributes at most k entries.",
